       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** The usual maximum is about 1,000 mg per dose, and 1,700 mg is well above that.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into doses\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg TID, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it."
